WIP / PoC: Add an nsenter friendly all-in-one inventory.

This patch series adds a containerized version of kolla-ansible as
built by the Kolla patch the series depends on. The container needs
to be able to run ansible tasks against the host it runs on, but
cannot rely on local access nor ssh to do that. Instead, it uses
the community.docker.nsenter connection plugin. The current all-in-one
inventory cannot be used for that with only its connection changed,
because it names the deploy host localhost.

This change adds all-in-one-deployer beside all-in-one. It differs only
in that:

* the deploy host is named kolla, so that every use of localhost stays
  in the container;
* ansible_connection=community.docker.nsenter in [all:vars] replaces
  ansible_connection=local on each host line; and
* ansible_remote_tmp is an absolute path. The nsenter plugin assumes
  that remote_user is root, and passes the container's environment,
  including HOME, to commands on the host, so the default
  ~/.ansible/tmp names a directory in the container's HOME, which the
  host does not have.

